{"name":"Mattar Paneer","hex":"#884433","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paneer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, non-matured, Indian cheese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paneer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Matar paneer","blocks":[{"text":"Mattar paneer, also known as matar paneer, muttar paneer, and mutter paneer, is a modern restaurant-style and vegetarian North Indian dish consisting of peas and paneer in a tomato-based sauce, spiced with garam masala."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Matar_paneer_dish.jpg/330px-Matar_paneer_dish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matar_paneer","wikidata":"Q6789614"},{"title":"Mattar","blocks":[{"text":"Mattar is an Arabic surname. People with that name include:"},{"items":["Ahmad Mattar, Singaporean politician","Mattar, Antônio Mattar Neto, Brazilian football player","Ali Mattar, Bahraini politician","Haitham Mattar, Lebanese-American business executive","Hassan Mattar,, Qatari football player","Luiz Mattar, Brazilian tennis player","Malak Mattar, Palestinian artist","Maurício Mattar,, Brazilian actor","Philip Mattar,, Palestinian-American historian","Spiridon Mattar (1921–2014), Melkite Greek Catholic Church leader"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mattar","wikidata":"Q37293015"},{"title":"Paneer","blocks":[{"text":"Paneer is a fresh acid-set cheese, common in South Asian cuisine, made from cow milk or buffalo milk. It is a non-aged, non-melting soft cheese made by curdling milk with an acid, such as lemon juice or citric acid. Paneer is predominantly used in north Indian dishes and is commonly used throughout South Asia, especially India, due to its versatility as an ingredient in diverse dishes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Panir_Paneer_Indian_cheese_fresh.jpg/330px-Panir_Paneer_Indian_cheese_fresh.jpg?utm_so